  "contracts": [
    "Review of the main-sidebar prerequisites found that ScrollBar::ObserveScrollEvent only updates feedback/scroll status. The Rust viewport previously consumed raw vertical events without moving content. The adapter now applies finite kScroll pixel deltas through Rust-owned offset/clamp state.",
    "Cocoa momentum kScroll updates use the same pixel path. Fling-start values remain velocities and never become position deltas. The OS retains momentum generation; this correction adds no custom physics.",
    "Horizontal-only ScrollEvent and MouseWheelEvent are not consumed by the vertical viewport. Vertical raw events are handled after applying their delta so Widget does not apply a synthesized wheel copy again.",
    "A dedicated Metal case routes fractional and momentum events through the real Widget::OnScrollEvent path after successful compositor presentation. It checks exact accumulated pixels, horizontal event propagation, velocity rejection, both extent clamps and content collapse. Two Rust model cases cover fractional/extreme deltas, invalid input and empty extents.",
    "Views implementation and browser-service/store/admission/persistence policy unchanged. No dependency added."
